&Q000491

{A.1 = 1-12}
11=1.	Lord of complex divine powers, who establishes umderstanding, whose intentions are unfathomable, who knows everything! 
17=2.	@wDN{Enki}, of broad wisdom, august ruler of the @wDN{Anuna}, wise one who casts spells, 
21=3.	who provides words, who attends to decisions, who clarifies verdicts, who dispenses advice from dawn to dusk! 
25=4.	@wDN{Enki}, lord of all true words, I will praise you. Your father, @wDN{An} the king, 
29=5.	the lord who caused human seed to come forth and who placed all mankind on the earth, 
33=6.	has laid upon you the guarding of the divine powers of heaven and earth, 
37=7.	and has elevated you to be their prince. @wDN{An}, king of the gods, 
41=8.	has instructed you to keep open the holy mouths of the @wWN{Tigris} and @wWN{Euphrates}, 
45=9.	to fill them with splendour, 
49=10.	to make the dense clouds release plentiful water and make them rain all over the fields, 
53=11.	to make @wDN{Ezina} lift her head in the furrows, to make vegetation …… in the desert, 
57=12.	and to make orchards and gardens ripe with syrup and vines grow as tall as forests. 

{A.13 = 13-20}
61=13.	@wDN{Enlil}, the lord who creates everything, has bestowed on you his august, proud and greatly awe-inspiring name: you are the junior @wDN{Enlil}. 
65=14.	Throughout heaven and earth he alone is divine, and you are his younger brother. 
69=15.	He has placed in your hands the power like him to decide destinies of both the south and the uplands. 
73=16.	A good decision that comes forth from your mouth is exceptionally powerful. 
77=17.	@wDN{Sa-bara} @noteref{a name of @wDN{Enlil} as judge}, you concern yourself with the sustenance of the people who are widely settled as far as the borders of the mountains: 
81=18.	you are their true father. 
85=19.	Lord, 
89=20.	all together they praise your greatness like the greatness of their protective deities. 

{A.21 = 21}
95=21.	@fsux{Sa-gida}. 

{B.22 = 22-23}
105=22.	@wDN{Nudimmud}, let your holy word and august command be a source of honour for @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, 
109=23.	and let him have no rivals. 

