115=24.	@fsux{Ŋišgiŋal. 

{C.25 = 25-34}
125=25.	August lord, you excel in heaven and earth, 
129=26.	and you have made your name shine forth. @wDN{Enki}, 
133=27.	you have gathered up all the divine powers that there are, and stored them in the @fsux{abzu}. 
137=28.	You have made praiseworthy the divine powers, exceeding all other divine powers, 
141=29.	of your holy dwelling which you have chosen in your heart -- the @fsux{abzu}, the august shrine …… -- as well as its divine plans. 
145=30.	Its shadow covers all lands from east to west, and its terrifying splendour rests upon the holy heavens like dense thunderclouds. 
149=31.	It fills with terror @wTN{E-kur}, the holy dwelling of @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil}. 
153=32.	Therein, equipped with the sceptre, 
157=33.	you fashion the numerous seeds (?) …… for the assigned divine powers of the great gods; to create mankind and to preserve them alive is in your power, 
161=34.	Father @wDN{Enki}, when you take your seat on the dais where you decide destinies. 

{C.35 = 35}
167=35.	@fsux{Sa-ŋara}. 

{D.36 = 36-47}
177=36.	May @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, the king in whom @wDN{Enlil} trusts, open up your house of wisdom in which you have gathered knowledge in plenty, 
181=37.	and then be the great ruler of the black-headed. Make terrifying splendour befitting his godhead issue from him, 
185=38.	the lion of kingship, in everything that he does, for as long as he lives. 
189=39.	May you present him with weighty tribute from the upper and the lower seas, 
193=40.	and let @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}} bring it into the glorious @wTN{E-kur}. May @wDN{Enlil} look upon him joyously, 
197=41.	and add to his period of rule blissful days and years of joy and life. 
201=42.	Father @wDN{Enki}, inspiring terrible awe, surpassing description, 
205=43.	may the @wDN{Anuna}, 
209=44.	your divine brothers, rejoice over you. 
213=45.	Son of @wDN{An}, 
217=46.	possessor of august honour, 
221=47.	it is sweet to praise you! 

